course: dictionary
lesson: 11447
title: Adipose tissue: the body's stored fat
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Adipose is a science word, and you can often work it out from the words around it. Scientists use it when they talk about the body. «Adipose tissue stores energy for the body.» Energy is stored, and the sentence is about the body, so adipose must be connected with body fat.
explain: «The nurse said the cells were adipose, full of fat.» The word full of fat is a clue. It tells you adipose means fatty. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Adipose words often appear in pairs, such as «adipose tissue» and «adipose cells». The first word is the one that matters most: tissue is the material in the body, and adipose tells you what kind of tissue it is. Look at the whole phrase, not just one word.
fact: Adipose means made of or about body fat.
fact: «Adipose tissue» is the fat stored in the body.
fact: Adipose tissue stores energy, keeps us warm and cushions our organs.
fact: «Adipose cells» are the cells that hold fat.
fact: Adipose is a formal and science word, so you will mostly meet it in biology and medicine, not in everyday talk.
exercise: «Adipose tissue stores energy for later.» What is adipose tissue? | Muscle used for running | Thin skin on the fingers | Bones that hold up the body | *Body fat that stores energy
exercise: «The nurse said the cells were adipose, full of fat.» What does adipose mean here? | Hard like bone | Watery | Very thin | *Fatty
exercise: «Adipose tissue helps to keep us ___.» Choose the right word to fill the gap. | asleep | *warm | cold | wet
test: «Adipose tissue cushions the organs inside the body.» What does cushions mean here? | Hurts | Counts | *Protects by padding | Heats
test: In «adipose tissue», which word is the noun? | Adipose | Both words | *Tissue | Neither word
exam: Why is adipose tissue useful to the body? | It makes the blood flow faster | *It stores energy and keeps us warm | It makes the bones grow longer | It helps us hear sounds
